  "python_code": "async def act(page):\n    \"\"\"\n    Steps:\n    - Use the site-aware helper create_curated_collection_by_search to perform a visible-site search for the keyword \"Collector\". This helper is the knowledge-base function designed for interacting with the complementary search widget and is therefore required to use.\n    - After the helper completes and search results are rendered into role=\"main\", locate the first role=\"article\" inside the main region and click the first meaningful link for that article. Prefer a link inside a heading; if none, click the first link in the article.\n\n    Notes:\n    - Every locator indexed with .nth() is preceded by an await .count() to avoid indexing errors.\n    - The click that navigates away is the last action in this function.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use the KB helper to perform the site search using the visible search UI.\n    # This helper navigates to '/' and activates the visible search widget.\n    await create_curated_collection_by_search(page, \"Collector\", max_results=0, resolve_links=True)\n\n    # After the search completes, find articles in the main region.\n    main = page.get_by_role(\"main\")\n    articles = main.get_by_role(\"article\")\n    articles_count = await articles.count()\n    if articles_count == 0:\n        # No search results found; nothing to click.\n        return\n\n    first_article = articles.nth(0)\n\n    # Prefer a link inside the article heading (if present).\n    heading = first_article.get_by_role(\"heading\")\n    heading_links = heading.get_by_role(\"link\")\n    heading_links_count = await heading_links.count()\n    if heading_links_count > 0:\n        await heading_links.nth(0).click()\n        return\n\n    # Fallback: click the first link inside the article.\n    article_links = first_article.get_by_role(\"link\")\n    article_links_count = await article_links.count()\n    if article_links_count > 0:\n        await article_links.nth(0).click()\n        return\n\n    # Nothing clickable found in the first article; done.\n    return\n",
